{"title":"Career Roadmap · Solar Technician","role":"Solar Technician","summary":"A Solar Technician installs, commissions, tests, maintains and troubleshoots solar photovoltaic (PV) systems. The role covers PV modules, inverters, wiring, electrical protection, batteries, mounting structures, monitoring systems and safety procedures.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Renewable Energy Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Renewable Energy Science → Solar Technician"},{"type":"p","text":"A Solar Technician installs, commissions, tests, maintains and troubleshoots solar photovoltaic (PV) systems. The role covers PV modules, inverters, wiring, electrical protection, batteries, mounting structures, monitoring systems and safety procedures."},{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for B.Sc Renewable Energy Science. For entry-level employment, practical installation and electrical skills are often more important than advanced academic qualifications."},{"type":"h","text":"Career facts"},{"type":"table","header":["Item","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Renewable Energy Science"}],[{"text":"Entry career"},{"text":"Solar Technician"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Renewable Energy · Solar PV · Electrical"}],[{"text":"Strongest foundations"},{"text":"Solar PV + electrical systems + electronics"}],[{"text":"Important field skills"},{"text":"Installation, wiring, testing, commissioning"}],[{"text":"Digital skills"},{"text":"Solar design software + monitoring + Excel"}],[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Electrical, rooftop and work-at-height safety"}],[{"text":"Long-term route"},{"text":"Solar Technician → Senior Technician → Site Supervisor → Solar Engineer/Manager"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Direct alignment","text":"Yes."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc graduate can target technician, installation, O&M and commissioning roles. However, some employers may prefer ITI/Diploma electrical backgrounds for technician-heavy positions, so the student should deliberately build practical electrical competence and certifications."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What should I focus on?"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build solar PV, electrical, electronics and installation skills alongside the B.Sc."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Become a skilled PV installation/O&M professional and specialise in rooftop, utility-scale, battery or solar-plus-storage systems."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress into Site Supervisor, Solar Design Engineer, O&M Engineer, Project Engineer or Technical Lead."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward Project Manager, Solar Operations Manager, Renewable Energy Consultant or technical entrepreneurship."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Electricity + basic electronics"},{"text":"University + practical labs"},{"text":"Wiring/electrical fundamentals"},{"text":"Electrical foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Solar energy fundamentals"},{"text":"NPTEL + PV training"},{"text":"PV system mini-project"},{"text":"Solar knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Solar PV components and systems"},{"text":"Lab + manufacturer training"},{"text":"Component identification/testing"},{"text":"Technical capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Installation + electrical protection"},{"text":"Practical training"},{"text":"Build a small PV system"},{"text":"Field readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"PV system design"},{"text":"PV software + field practice"},{"text":"Complete rooftop design"},{"text":"Design skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Solar internship"},{"text":"EPC/O&M company"},{"text":"Installation/O&M logbook"},{"text":"Industry exposure"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Commissioning + troubleshooting"},{"text":"Manufacturer manuals + field work"},{"text":"Commissioning checklist"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Advanced solar/storage project"},{"text":"Industry mentor"},{"text":"Complete solar project portfolio"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"If the B.Sc. is a 3-year programme, compress the Year 4 activities into the final year."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"h","text":"Renewable energy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Solar Energy"},{"text":"Solar Radiation"},{"text":"Solar PV Technology"},{"text":"Solar Thermal Systems"},{"text":"Renewable Energy Systems"},{"text":"Energy Conversion"},{"text":"Energy Storage"},{"text":"Energy Management"},{"text":"Energy Economics"},{"text":"Renewable Energy Policy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Electrical fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electrical circuits"},{"text":"AC/DC systems"},{"text":"Electrical machines"},{"text":"Power electronics"},{"text":"Transformers"},{"text":"Electrical measurements"},{"text":"Earthing"},{"text":"Protection systems"},{"text":"Power distribution"},{"text":"Electrical safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Solar PV"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PV cell physics"},{"text":"Solar modules"},{"text":"Module configurations"},{"text":"Series/parallel connections"},{"text":"DC systems"},{"text":"Inverters"},{"text":"MPPT"},{"text":"Charge controllers"},{"text":"DC/AC protection"},{"text":"Combiner boxes"},{"text":"Cables and connectors"},{"text":"Mounting structures"},{"text":"Rooftop systems"},{"text":"Ground-mounted systems"},{"text":"Grid-connected systems"},{"text":"Off-grid systems"},{"text":"Hybrid systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical and field skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Solar installation"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","ite